DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       pprreeaadd()  reads up to _c_o_u_n_t bytes from file descriptor _f_d at offset _o_f_f_‐
       _s_e_t (from the start of the file) into the buffer starting at _b_u_f.   The
       file offset is not changed.

       ppwwrriittee()  writes  up  to _c_o_u_n_t bytes from the buffer starting at _b_u_f to
       the file descriptor _f_d at  offset  _o_f_f_s_e_t.   The  file  offset  is  not
       changed.

       The file referenced by _f_d must be capable of seeking.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On  success, pprreeaadd() returns the number of bytes read (a return of zero
       indicates end of file) and ppwwrriittee() returns the number of  bytes  writ‐
       ten.

       Note  that  it  is not an error for a successful call to transfer fewer
       bytes than requested (see rreeaadd(2) and wwrriittee(2)).

       On error, -1 is returned and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

